On Sun, Nov 10, 2013 at 12:18 AM, Wuzzy <almikes@aol.com> wrote:

> Hi!
> I want to start a little survey about how people
> learn the basic vocabulary of Lojban. I do this just out
> of curiosity, that=92s all.
>
> If you want to participate, just reply to this e-mail and
> answer these questions:
> 1) Did you learn any Lojban vocabulary so far?
>

Yes

If you said =93no=94, the survey is done for you. If you said =93yes=94, go=
 on:
> 2) How many of the gismu do you have memorized right now?
>

  Well, it depends on your definition.  If you mean knowing the x1 and
(where applicable) x2 places, then ALL of the non-experimental gismu, even
the piddling  ones that I will never have occasion to use, like gocti,
stero, gotro and delno.  For the further places, slightly less.


> 3) How many rafsi?
>

  About three thousand.  Oh, did you mean only the 3 letter ones?  Then
probably about 300.  The majority of those because of the lujvo vocabulary,
and my interpreting of English/other language words, names, etc, as lojban,
or the anagramming of English phrases and names as lojban utterances.


> 4) And how many cmavo?
>

  There was a time that I could have said 100%, but now it's probably down
to 75% or so.  My main problems are probably evidentials, obscure BY and PA
subsetss, and underused-by-me BAI and tenses (like I can never remember if
"zo'i" is "in" our "out").


> 5) When did you start learning vocabulary?
>

2004


> 6) How often (roughly) do (or did) you learn?
>

   I go back to memrise when I come across the email reminder, probably
about once a week, or more often (once or twice a day) in irregular spurts
of motivation

7) On a regular basis?
>

  (see above)


> 8) Which learning tool or learning method do you use?
>

  I use memrise currently, I used to use the defunct rememberize  also from
my own printed sheets from Robin's "big list" page. (modified to my own
"braste" document)

Extra question for those who already memorized all gismu, rafsi and cmavo:
> 9) When did you =93make it=94? (a rough estimate)
>
> Notes: I only talk about the _official_ gismu, cmavo and rafsi.
> Knowledge of other valsi or rafsi is not relevant to this survey.
> With =93memorized=94 I mean something like: I throw you out of bed and as=
k you
> =93Quick! What=92s the definition of =91jalge=92?=94 then you automatical=
ly,
> while still not really awake, can say the correct answer.
>
>
        --gejyspa

